{"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1637357?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1637357?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1637357?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1637357?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1637357?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1637357?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1637357"},"revision_id":109,"created":"2017-11-22T00:00:00+00:00","updated":"2023-03-07T04:13:12.640294+00:00","uuid":"0b45b148-76b7-458e-9080-448a1c6090aa","id":"1637357","metadata":{"citation_count":67,"citation_count_without_self_citations":66,"urls":[{"value":"https://www.quantamagazine.org/to-test-einsteins-equations-poke-a-black-hole-20180308/","description":"Quanta Magazine article"}],"titles":[{"title":"Global Nonlinear Stability of Schwarzschild Spacetime under Polarized Perturbations","source":"arXiv"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","authors":[{"uuid":"42229797-f1b6-4486-95d9-96b7f046aaff","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1050880"},"full_name":"Klainerman, Sergiu","signature_block":"CLANARNANs"},{"uuid":"b1f4c12b-6959-40f4-82a1-c60b3fff29e4","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2133496"},"full_name":"Szeftel, Jeremie","signature_block":"SAFTALj"}],"curated":false,"figures":[{"key":"50368360278846695e7ea4ae75aa715e","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/50368360278846695e7ea4ae75aa715e","source":"arxiv","caption":"The GCM admissible space-time $\\mathcal{M}$","filename":"spacetimepicturenew.png"},{"key":"32bf3043e7c113844634ea384f756247","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/32bf3043e7c113844634ea384f756247","source":"arxiv","caption":"The Penrose diagram of the space-time $\\mathcal{M}$","filename":"penrosediagramconclusion.png"},{"key":"b70f91764b3e849e7728ccb5dee0bcc8","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/b70f91764b3e849e7728ccb5dee0bcc8","source":"arxiv","caption":"The initial data layer $\\LL_0$","filename":"initialdatalayerfigure.png"}],"license":[{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint"},{"url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/","imposing":"arXiv"}],"texkeys":["Klainerman:2017nrb"],"citeable":true,"abstracts":[{"value":"We prove the nonlinear stability of the Schwarzschild spacetime under axially symmetric polarized perturbations, i.e. solutions of the Einstein vacuum equations for asymptotically flat $1+3$ dimensional Lorentzian metrics which admit a hypersurface orthogonal spacelike Killing vectorfield with closed orbits. While building on the remarkable advances made in last 15 years on establishing quantitative linear stability, the paper introduces a series of new ideas among which we emphasize the general covariant modulation (GCM) procedure which allows us to construct, dynamically, the center of mass frame of the final state. The mass of the final state itself is tracked using the well known Hawking mass relative to a well adapted foliation itself connected to the center of mass frame. Our work here is the first to prove the nonlinear stability of Schwarzschild in a restricted class of nontrivial perturbations. To a large extent, the restriction to this class of perturbations is only needed to ensure that the final state of evolution is another Schwarzschild space. We are thus confident that our procedure may apply in a more general setting.","source":"arXiv"}],"references":[{"raw_refs":[{"value":"[1] S. Aksteiner, private communication.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["private communication"],"label":"1","authors":[{"full_name":"Aksteiner, S."}]}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1500179"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[2] S. Aksteiner, L. Andersson, T. B¨ ackdahl, A. G. Shah and B. F. Whiting, Gaugeinvariant perturbations of Schwarzschild spacetime, arXiv.1611.08291.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["Gaugeinvariant perturbations of Schwarzschild spacetime, arXiv"],"label":"2","authors":[{"full_name":"Aksteiner, S."},{"full_name":"Andersson, L."},{"full_name":"Bäckdahl, T."},{"full_name":"Shah, A.G."},{"full_name":"Whiting, B.F."}],"arxiv_eprint":"1611.08291"},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/829056"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[3] L. Andersson and P. Blue, Hidden symmetries and decay for the wave equation on the Kerr spacetime, arXiv:0908.2265, to appear in Annals of Math.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["Hidden symmetries and decay for the wave equation on the Kerr spacetime / to appear in Annals of Math"],"label":"3","authors":[{"full_name":"Andersson, L."},{"full_name":"Blue, P."}],"arxiv_eprint":"0908.2265"},"curated_relation":false},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1501915"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[4] Y. Angelopoulos, S. Aretakis and D. Gajic, A vector field approach to almostsharp decay for the wave equation on spherically symmetric, stationary spacetimes, arXiv:1612.01565.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["A vector field approach to almostsharp decay for the wave equation on spherically symmetric, stationary spacetimes"],"label":"4","authors":[{"full_name":"Angelopoulos, Y."},{"full_name":"Aretakis, S."},{"full_name":"Gajic, D."}],"arxiv_eprint":"1612.01565"},"curated_relation":false},{"raw_refs":[{"value":"[5] J. M. Bardeen and W. H. Press, Radiation fields in the Schwarzschild background, J. Math. Phys., 14 (1973), pp. 719.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["Radiation fields in the Schwarzschild background"],"label":"5","authors":[{"full_name":"Bardeen, J.M."},{"full_name":"Press, W.H."}],"publication_info":{"year":1973,"artid":"719","page_start":"719","journal_title":"J.Math.Phys.","journal_volume":"14"}}},{"raw_refs":[{"value":"[6] L. Bieri, An extension of the stability theorem of the Minkowski space in general relativity, Thesis, ETH, 2007.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["An extension of the stability theorem of the Minkowski space in Thesis, ETH"],"label":"6","title":{"title":"General relativity"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Bieri, L."}],"publication_info":{"year":2007}}},{"raw_refs":[{"value":"[7] P. Blue and A. Soffer, Semilinear wave equations on the Schwarzschild manifold. I. Local decay estimates, Adv. Differential Equations 8 (2003), 595–614.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["Semilinear wave equations on the Schwarzschild manifold. I. Local / decay estimates, Adv"],"label":"7","authors":[{"full_name":"Blue, P."},{"full_name":"Soffer, A."}],"publication_info":{"year":2003,"page_end":"614","page_start":"595","journal_title":"Diff.Eq.","journal_volume":"8"}}},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/723839"},"raw_refs":[{"value":"[8] P. Blue and A. Soffer, Errata for “Global existence and scattering for the nonlinear Schr¨ odinger equation on Schwarzschild manifolds” , “Semilinear wave equations on the Schwarzschild manifold I: Local Decay Estimates”, and “ The wave equation on the Schwarzschild metric II: Local Decay for the spin 2 Regge Wheeler equation” , gr-qc/0608073, 6 pages.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["Errata for / and / 6 pages"],"label":"8","title":{"title":"The wave equation on the Schwarzschild metric II: Local Decay for the spin 2 Regge Wheeler equation"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Blue, P."},{"full_name":"Soffer, A."}],"arxiv_eprint":"gr-qc/0608073"},"curated_relation":false},{"raw_refs":[{"value":"[9] P. Blue and A. Soffer, A space-time integral estimate for a large data semi-linear wave equation on the Schwarzschild manifold, Lett. Math. Phys, 81 (2007), 227–238.","schema":"text"}],"reference":{"misc":["A space-time integral estimate for a large data semi-linear wave equation on the Schwarzschild manifold"],"label":"9","authors":[{"full_name":"Blue, P."},{"full_na